Project Summary: Multi-Platform Bot Messaging System
🎯 Goal

Build a reliable messaging + alert system for bots and system monitoring that does NOT depend on Telegram as the primary infrastructure.

Telegram is used only as an optional distribution channel.

🏗️ Core Architecture
1. Primary system (source of truth)

Use Matrix via Element

Element

This is the main hub for all bot messages
All alerts, logs, and system notifications are sent here first
Can be self-hosted or use public Matrix servers
Must support:
bot posting messages
multiple rooms (e.g. alerts, logs, admin)
2. Optional distribution layer
Telegram (secondary output only)

Telegram

Used ONLY for user reach / convenience
Not trusted as source of truth
Messages are forwarded from Matrix → Telegram
Must tolerate:
broken links
group changes
inconsistent availability
3. Bridge / fan-out layer

Two acceptable approaches:

Option A (preferred): Matrix-native bridges
Matrix room is canonical
Bridges sync messages outward to Telegram/Discord
Example: Matrix ↔ Telegram bridge
Option B: Bot fan-out system
Single bot sends messages to:
Matrix room (primary)
Telegram Bot API (secondary)
Simpler but less “clean”
🤖 Bot Requirements

Bots should:

Send messages to Matrix room as primary output
Format messages consistently:
timestamp
source system
severity (INFO / WARN / ERROR)
Support multiple event types:
system alerts
monitoring pings
custom events
Be resilient (retry on failure, queue if needed)
🧱 Suggested Implementation Stack
Backend
Python or Node.js (choose one consistent stack)
HTTP webhook ingestion OR direct function calls
Matrix integration
Matrix bot client library (or simple Matrix HTTP API client)
Telegram integration (optional)
Telegram Bot API (for posting only, not logic)
🔄 Message Flow
Bots / Monitoring Systems
        ↓
   Core Bot Service
        ↓
   Matrix Room (PRIMARY)
        ↓
   ├── Telegram (optional forward)
   └── future platforms (Discord, etc.)
🧠 Key Design Principles
Matrix is the source of truth
Telegram is a best-effort mirror
No platform lock-in
System must function even if Telegram is broken/unavailable
Avoid dependence on any single messaging provider
🧩 Optional Expansion (future)
Discord bridge
Web dashboard for logs
Multiple Matrix rooms per system (prod / dev / alerts)
Persistent event storage (SQLite/Postgres)
🚀 MVP Scope (build first)
Simple bot that can:
receive event (HTTP or function call)
send to Matrix room
Optional module:
forward same message to Telegram bot
Basic formatting + logging
